pan></td></tr><tr class="item"><td><code>erfinv(y)</code></td><td>Inverse error function: erf(erfinv(y)) = y, -1 &lt; y &lt; 1.<br><span class="ex">e.g. <code>erfinv(0.5)</code></span></td></tr><tr class="item"><td><code>normcdf(x)<br>normcdf(x, mu, sigma)</code></td><td>Normal cumulative probability (standard normal if mu and sigma are left out).<br><span class="ex">e.g. <code>normcdf(1.96)</code></span></td></tr><tr class="item"><td><code>norminv(p)<br>norminv(p, mu, sigma)</code></td><td>Inverse of normcdf: the value below which the probability is p.<br><span class="ex">e.g. <code>norminv(0.975)</code></span></td></tr><tr class="item"><td><code>tcdf(t, nu)</code></td><td>Student's t cumulative probability with nu degrees of freedom.<br><span class="ex">e.g. <code>tcdf(2.262, 9)</code></span></td></tr><tr class="item"><td><code>tinv(p, nu)</code></td><td>Inverse of tcdf. tinv(0.975, nu) is the coverage factor for a 95 % two-sided interval.<br><span class="ex">e.g. <code>tinv(0.975, 9)</code></span></td></tr></tbody></table>
